content.text:
The surface needed no changes for these six scenarios, so `h.d.ts`, `kernel.d.ts` and `design.md` are not re-emitted. Each scenario below is written against the surface exactly as given.

Interpretations worth checking:

- **Scenario 2, rejected drafts.** A reviewer's rejection feeds a redraft loop of at most three rounds, carrying the reviewer's notes. A draft still unapproved after three rounds ends the conversation in `Escalated`.
- **Scenario 2, the Escalation unit.** One trigger on the transition into `Escalated` creates the Escalation unit, whatever the cause. The SLA timer only signals that transition, so the breach reaches the Escalation lane through two recorded triggers rather than one.
- **Scenario 2, customer replies.** A reply cancels any open attempt and returns the unit to `New`, not only during approval. That also covers a reply after `Sent`.
- **Scenario 3, weekly re-open.** The re-open timer counts from the unit's creation time. A topic created on a Monday morning and delivered within the hour could therefore re-open the same day.
- **Scenario 6, returned drafts.** `Returned` is terminal with verdict failure. A resubmitted draft arrives through the CMS poll as a fresh unit under the same key.
- **Scenario 6, fact-check output.** The fact-check command reports at most one repeat mistake per run, because a trigger records one memory item per firing.

=== FILE: scenarios/01-coding-team.ts ===
import { z } from 'zod';
import { H } from 'harness-dsl';
import { linear } from 'harness-dsl/linear';
import type { LinearIssue } from 'harness-dsl/linear';
import { folder } from 'harness-dsl/folder';
import { claudeCode } from 'harness-dsl/claude-code';
import { anthropic } from 'harness-dsl/anthropic';
import { sqlite } from 'harness-dsl/sqlite';
import { jsonl } from 'harness-dsl/jsonl';
import { git } from 'harness-dsl/git';
import { local } from 'harness-dsl/local';
import { markdown } from 'harness-dsl/markdown';

const areaSchema = z.enum(['payments', 'checkout', 'platform']);
type Area = z.infer<typeof areaSchema>;
const workItem = z.object({ ref: z.string(), title: z.string(), body: z.string(), area: areaSchema });
type WorkItem = z.infer<typeof workItem>;
const epicItem = z.object({ ref: z.string(), title: z.string(), body: z.string() });
const heartbeatItem = z.object({ service: z.string() });

const areaResources = {
  payments: H.resource('payments'),
  checkout: H.resource('checkout'),
  platform: H.resource('platform'),
};
const areaOf = (labels: readonly string[]): Area =>
  labels.includes('payments') ? 'payments' : labels.includes('checkout') ? 'checkout' : 'platform';
const issueItem = (issue: LinearIssue): WorkItem => ({
  ref: issue.identifier,
  title: issue.title,
  body: issue.description,
  area: areaOf(issue.labels),
});

const Todo = H.state('Todo', 'pending');
const Triage = H.state('Triage', 'waiting');
const Done = H.terminal('Done', 'success');
const Abandoned = H.terminal('Abandoned', 'failure');
const Canceled = H.terminal('Canceled', 'neutral');
const Due = H.state('Due', 'pending');
const Healthy = H.terminal('Healthy', 'success');
const Unhealthy = H.terminal('Unhealthy', 'failure');

const Bug = H.kind('Bug').attributes(workItem).states(Todo, Triage, Done, Abandoned, Canceled).key(a => a.ref);
const Feature = H.kind('Feature').attributes(workItem).states(Todo, Triage, Done, Abandoned, Canceled).key(a => a.ref);
const Epic = H.kind('Epic').attributes(epicItem).states(Todo, Triage, Done, Abandoned, Canceled).key(a => a.ref);
const Heartbeat = H.kind('ServiceHeartbeat').attributes(heartbeatItem).states(Due, Healthy, Unhealthy).key(a => a.service);

const quota = sqlite.quota('claude-accounts', { path: '.harness/quota.db' });
const subscriptionA = claudeCode.subscription('subscription-a', { token: H.env('CLAUDE_TOKEN_A'), quota });
const subscriptionB = claudeCode.subscription('subscription-b', { token: H.env('CLAUDE_TOKEN_B'), quota });
const subscriptionC = claudeCode.subscription('subscription-c', { token: H.env('CLAUDE_TOKEN_C'), quota });
const apiAccount = anthropic.account('api-fallback', { apiKey: H.env('ANTHROPIC_API_KEY'), quota });

const soonestExpiring = H.policy.account('soonest-expiring-first', ({ candidates, now }) =>
  [...candidates]
    .filter(c => c.shareUsed < c.shareCap && (c.cooldownUntil === undefined || c.cooldownUntil.getTime() <= now.getTime()))
    .sort((a, b) => a.windowResetsAt.getTime() - b.windowResetsAt.getTime())[0]);

const subscriptions = H.pool('subscriptions')
  .accounts(subscriptionA, subscriptionB, subscriptionC)
  .share(subscriptionA, 0.5)
  .share(subscriptionB, 0.5)
  .share(subscriptionC, 0.3)
  .drain(soonestExpiring)
  .fallback(apiAccount);

const sonnet = claudeCode.model('sonnet', { id: 'claude-sonnet-4-5' });
const opus = claudeCode.model('opus', { id: 'claude-opus-4-5' });

const builderModel = H.policy.model('builder-model', [sonnet, opus], ({ kind, seat, metrics }) => {
  const cheaper = metrics.attempts({ of: kind, seat, model: sonnet, window: { lastDays: 14 } });
  return cheaper.samples >= 20 && cheaper.successRate < 0.85 ? opus : sonnet;
});

const builder = H.role('builder')
  .intents('read', 'edit', 'run', 'search')
  .instructions('Implement the task. Address every deficit from earlier rounds. If an owner decision is needed, put it in question.');
const auditor = H.role('auditor')
  .intents('read', 'run', 'record')
  .instructions('Find deficits in the change. Report none only when the work is complete.');
const planner = H.role('planner')
  .intents('read', 'search')
  .instructions('Decompose the epic into independently deliverable features.');

const localRunner = local.runner('local').slots(4);
const projectChecks = H.command('project-checks').argv(['npm', 'run', 'check']).runner(localRunner);
const probeService = H.command('probe-service')
  .input(heartbeatItem)
  .argv(i => ['./scripts/probe', i.service])
  .output(z.object({ healthy: z.boolean(), detail: z.string() }))
  .runner(localRunner);
const probeProduction = H.command('probe-production')
  .argv(['./scripts/probe-production'])
  .output(z.object({ healthy: z.boolean(), detail: z.string() }))
  .runner(localRunner);

const worktree = git.worktree({ repo: '.', base: 'main' });

const builderSeat = H.seat('builder')
  .role(builder)
  .model(builderModel)
  .pool(subscriptions)
  .output(z.object({ summary: z.string(), question: z.string().optional() }))
  .workspace(worktree, { leaseFiles: true, beforeStop: projectChecks });

const auditorSeat = H.seat('auditor')
  .role(auditor)
  .model(opus)
  .pool(subscriptions)
  .output(z.object({ deficits: z.array(z.object({ file: z.string(), problem: z.string() })) }))
  .workspace(worktree);

const plannerSeat = H.seat('planner')
  .role(planner)
  .model(opus)
  .pool(subscriptions)
  .output(z.object({ features: z.array(z.object({ slug: z.string(), title: z.string(), body: z.string(), area: areaSchema })) }));

const ownerDecision = H.halt('owner-decision').decision(z.object({ answer: z.string() }));

const deliver = H.flow('deliver')
  .input(workItem)
  .params(z.object({ rounds: z.number() }))
  .loop(
    'rounds',
    z.object({ deficits: z.array(z.string()), ownerAnswer: z.string().optional() }),
    body => body
      .step('build', builderSeat, ctx => ({
        task: [
          ctx.unit.attributes.title,
          ctx.unit.attributes.body,
          ...ctx.steps.rounds.map((round, index) =>
            `Round ${index + 1} deficits: ${round.deficits.join('; ')}${round.ownerAnswer ? `. Owner answered: ${round.ownerAnswer}` : ''}`),
        ].join('\n\n'),
        resources: [areaResources[ctx.unit.attributes.area]],
      }))
      .halt('askOwner', ownerDecision, {
        when: ctx => ctx.steps.build.question !== undefined,
        ask: ctx => ctx.steps.build.question ?? '',
      })
      .step('audit', auditorSeat, ctx => ({
        task: `Audit the change for "${ctx.unit.attributes.title}". Builder summary: ${ctx.steps.build.summary}${ctx.steps.askOwner ? `. Owner decided: ${ctx.steps.askOwner.answer}` : ''}`,
        resources: [areaResources[ctx.unit.attributes.area]],
      })),
    {
      max: ctx => ctx.params.rounds,
      until: ctx => ctx.steps.audit.deficits.length === 0,
      feed: ctx => ({
        deficits: ctx.steps.audit.deficits.map(d => `${d.file}: ${d.problem}`),
        ownerAnswer: ctx.steps.askOwner?.answer,
      }),
    },
  )
  .exit('clean', ctx => ctx.steps.audit.deficits.length === 0)
  .exit('unresolved');

const heartbeatFlow = H.flow('heartbeat')
  .input(heartbeatItem)
  .step('probe', probeService, ctx => ({ service: ctx.unit.attributes.service }))
  .exit('healthy', ctx => ctx.steps.probe.healthy)
  .exit('unhealthy');

const linearKey = H.env('LINEAR_API_KEY');
const tracker = linear.store({
  apiKey: linearKey,
  team: 'ENG',
  workflow: ['Todo', 'In Progress', 'Triage', 'Done', 'Canceled'],
});

const bugs = H.lane('bugs', Bug)
  .supply(linear.issues({ apiKey: linearKey, team: 'ENG', labels: ['bug'] }), (issue, to) => to.create(issueItem(issue)))
  .supply(folder.files({ path: 'bugs', glob: '*.md' }), (file, to) =>
    to.create({ ref: `file:${file.name}`, title: file.name, body: file.body, area: 'platform' }))
  .supply(H.operator)
  .store(tracker, {
    states: { Todo: 'Todo', Triage: 'Triage', Done: 'Done', Abandoned: 'Canceled', Canceled: 'Canceled' },
    inFlight: 'In Progress',
  })
  .handler(deliver, { exits: { clean: Done, unresolved: Triage }, params: { rounds: 3 } })
  .retry({ maxAttempts: 2, backoff: 'exponential', initialDelayMs: 60000, exhausted: Abandoned })
  .on(H.cancel, { enter: Canceled });

const features = H.lane('features', Feature)
  .supply(linear.issues({ apiKey: linearKey, team: 'ENG', labels: ['feature'] }), (issue, to) => to.create(issueItem(issue)))
  .supply(H.operator)
  .store(tracker, {
    states: { Todo: 'Todo', Triage: 'Triage', Done: 'Done', Abandoned: 'Canceled', Canceled: 'Canceled' },
    inFlight: 'In Progress',
  })
  .handler(deliver, { exits: { clean: Done, unresolved: Triage }, params: { rounds: 5 } })
  .retry({ maxAttempts: 2, backoff: 'exponential', initialDelayMs: 60000, exhausted: Abandoned })
  .on(H.cancel, { enter: Canceled });

const planEpic = H.flow('plan-epic')
  .input(epicItem)
  .step('plan', plannerSeat, ctx => ({
    task: `Decompose this epic into features.\n\n${ctx.unit.attributes.title}\n\n${ctx.unit.attributes.body}`,
  }))
  .spawn('features', features, (ctx): WorkItem[] =>
    ctx.steps.plan.features.map(f => ({
      ref: `${ctx.unit.attributes.ref}/${f.slug}`,
      title: f.title,
      body: f.body,
      area: f.area,
    })))
  .exit('complete', ctx => ctx.steps.features.every(child => child.verdict === 'success'))
  .exit('incomplete');

const epics = H.lane('epics', Epic)
  .supply(linear.issues({ apiKey: linearKey, team: 'ENG', labels: ['epic'] }), (issue, to) =>
    to.create({ ref: issue.identifier, title: issue.title, body: issue.description }))
  .store(tracker, {
    states: { Todo: 'Todo', Triage: 'Triage', Done: 'Done', Abandoned: 'Canceled', Canceled: 'Canceled' },
    inFlight: 'In Progress',
  })
  .handler(planEpic, { exits: { complete: Done, incomplete: Triage } })
  .retry({ maxAttempts: 2, backoff: 'exponential', initialDelayMs: 60000, exhausted: Abandoned })
  .on(H.cancel, { enter: Canceled });

const services = ['checkout-api', 'payments-api', 'web'];

const heartbeats = H.lane('heartbeats', Heartbeat)
  .supply(H.clock('every-five-minutes').every({ minutes: 5 }), (_tick, to) => services.map(service => to.create({ service })))
  .handler(heartbeatFlow, { exits: { healthy: Healthy, unhealthy: Unhealthy } })
  .retry({ maxAttempts: 1, exhausted: Unhealthy });

const heartbeatFailure = H.trigger('failed-heartbeat-files-bug')
  .on(H.when.transition(heartbeats, { to: Unhealthy }))
  .create(bugs, (event): WorkItem => ({
    ref: `heartbeat:${event.unit.attributes.service}`,
    title: `${event.unit.attributes.service} heartbeat failed`,
    body: `The heartbeat for ${event.unit.attributes.service} failed at ${event.at.toISOString()}.`,
    area: 'platform',
  }));

const experienceJournal = H.journal('coding-experience', H.memory('experience', 'experience'))
  .store(jsonl.memoryStore({ path: '.harness/experience.jsonl' }))
  .recall({ by: 'specificity', limit: 12 })
  .readBy(builder, auditor)
  .recordedBy(auditor);

const tasteJournal = H.journal('owner-taste', H.memory('taste', 'taste'))
  .store(jsonl.memoryStore({ path: '.harness/taste.jsonl' }))
  .recall({ by: 'specificity', limit: 12 })
  .readBy(builder, planner);

const scheduler = H.scheduler('coding-team')
  .standard(heartbeats, bugs, features, epics)
  .wip(bugs, 2)
  .wip(epics, 1)
  .aging(features, { afterMinutes: 240 });

const supervisor = claudeCode.supervisor('supervisor', {
  port: H.slot.port(1),
  grants: [
    H.ops.workRead,
    H.ops.workCreate,
    H.ops.workUpdate,
    H.ops.workCancel,
    H.ops.resolve(ownerDecision),
    H.ops.memoryWrite,
    H.ops.telemetryRead,
    H.ops.accountsShare,
    H.operation('production-health-probe', probeProduction),
  ],
});

const harness = H.harness('coding-team')
  .ledger(sqlite.ledger({ path: '.harness/ledger.db' }))
  .lanes(heartbeats, bugs, features, epics)
  .journals(experienceJournal, tasteJournal)
  .triggers(heartbeatFailure)
  .scheduler(scheduler)
  .clients(supervisor)
  .observers(markdown.board({ path: 'BOARD.md' }), markdown.telemetry({ path: 'TELEMETRY.md' }));

void harness.start();
=== END ===

=== FILE: scenarios/02-support-triage.ts ===
import { z } from 'zod';
import { H } from 'harness-dsl';
import type { Router, Route } from 'harness-dsl';
import { zendesk } from 'harness-dsl/zendesk';
import type { ZendeskEvent } from 'harness-dsl/zendesk';
import { anthropic } from 'harness-dsl/anthropic';
import { sqlite } from 'harness-dsl/sqlite';
import { jsonl } from 'harness-dsl/jsonl';
import { local } from 'harness-dsl/local';
import { claudeCode } from 'harness-dsl/claude-code';
import { markdown } from 'harness-dsl/markdown';

const conversation = z.object({
  ticketId: z.string(),
  subject: z.string(),
  message: z.string(),
  customerEmail: z.string(),
  slaDeadline: z.string(),
  escalationReason: z.string().optional(),
});
type ConversationAttrs = z.infer<typeof conversation>;
const escalation = z.object({ ticketId: z.string(), subject: z.string(), reason: z.string() });

const categories = z.enum(['billing', 'refund', 'technical', 'account', 'other']);
const category = H.facet('category', categories);

const New = H.state('New', 'pending');
const Sent = H.state('Sent', 'waiting');
const ClosedByCustomer = H.terminal('ClosedByCustomer', 'success');
const Escalated = H.terminal('Escalated', 'failure');
const Conversation = H.kind('Conversation')
  .attributes(conversation)
  .states(New, Sent, ClosedByCustomer, Escalated)
  .key(a => a.ticketId);

const EscalationOpen = H.state('EscalationOpen', 'pending');
const EscalationHandled = H.terminal('EscalationHandled', 'success');
const EscalationDropped = H.terminal('EscalationDropped', 'failure');
const Escalation = H.kind('Escalation')
  .attributes(escalation)
  .states(EscalationOpen, EscalationHandled, EscalationDropped)
  .key(a => a.ticketId);

const customerReplied = H.signal('customer-replied').payload(z.object({ message: z.string() }));
const customerClosed = H.signal('customer-closed');
const slaBreached = H.signal('sla-breached');

const slaHours = { low: 48, normal: 24, high: 8, urgent: 2 };

const routeTicket = (event: ZendeskEvent, to: Router<ConversationAttrs>): Route => {
  if (event.status === 'solved' || event.status === 'closed') return to.signal(customerClosed, event.ticketId, {});
  if (event.type === 'created') {
    return to.create({
      ticketId: event.ticketId,
      subject: event.subject,
      message: event.message,
      customerEmail: event.customerEmail,
      slaDeadline: new Date(event.createdAt.getTime() + slaHours[event.priority] * 3600000).toISOString(),
    });
  }
  if (event.type === 'replied') return to.signal(customerReplied, event.ticketId, { message: event.message });
  return to.skip();
};

const quota = sqlite.quota('support-quota', { path: '.harness/quota.db' });
const apiAccount = anthropic.account('support-api', { apiKey: H.env('ANTHROPIC_API_KEY'), quota });
const api = H.pool('support-api').accounts(apiAccount);
const haiku = anthropic.model('haiku', { id: 'claude-haiku-4-5' });
const sonnet = anthropic.model('sonnet', { id: 'claude-sonnet-4-5' });

const classifier = H.role('classifier').intents('read').instructions('Classify the conversation into one category.');
const drafter = H.role('drafter').intents('read').instructions('Draft a reply in the house tone, addressing every point the customer raised.');
const reviewer = H.role('reviewer');

const classifierSeat = H.seat('classifier').role(classifier).model(haiku).pool(api).output(z.object({ category: categories }));
const drafterSeat = H.seat('drafter').role(drafter).model(sonnet).pool(api).output(z.object({ reply: z.string() }));

const approval = H.halt('reply-approval').decision(z.object({
  approved: z.boolean(),
  editedReply: z.string().optional(),
  notes: z.string().optional(),
}));
const costCeiling = H.halt('conversation-cost').decision(H.ceilingDecision);
const escalationHandled = H.halt('escalation-handled').decision(z.object({
  outcome: z.enum(['handled', 'dropped']),
  notes: z.string(),
}));

const approvals = H.metric('reply-approvals', H.when.decision(Conversation, approval)).samples(event =>
  event.resolvedBy === 'human'
    ? [{ hit: event.decision.approved, facets: event.facets, seat: drafterSeat, model: event.modelOf(drafterSeat) }]
    : []);

const safeCategory = H.policy.halt('safe-category-skips-approval', Conversation, approval, ({ facets, metrics }) => {
  const record = metrics.rate(approvals, { facets });
  return record.samples >= 200 && record.hits === record.samples ? { approved: true } : undefined;
});

const sendReply = H.command('send-reply')
  .input(z.object({ ticketId: z.string(), reply: z.string() }))
  .argv(i => ['./bin/helpdesk-reply', '--ticket', i.ticketId, '--body', i.reply])
  .runner(local.runner('local'));

const reply = H.flow('reply')
  .input(conversation)
  .step('classify', classifierSeat, ctx => ({
    task: `Classify this conversation.\n\n${ctx.unit.attributes.subject}\n\n${ctx.unit.attributes.message}`,
  }))
  .loop(
    'drafts',
    z.object({ draft: z.string(), notes: z.string() }),
    body => body
      .step('draft', drafterSeat, ctx => ({
        task: [
          `Draft a reply to this ${ctx.steps.classify.category} conversation.`,
          ctx.unit.attributes.message,
          ...ctx.steps.drafts.map(d => `A reviewer rejected:\n${d.draft}\nNotes: ${d.notes}`),
        ].join('\n\n'),
        skills: [ctx.steps.classify.category],
      }))
      .halt('approve', approval, {
        ask: ctx => ctx.steps.draft.reply,
        skip: safeCategory,
        facets: ctx => [category.of(ctx.steps.classify.category)],
      }),
    {
      max: 3,
      until: ctx => ctx.steps.approve.approved,
      feed: ctx => ({ draft: ctx.steps.draft.reply, notes: ctx.steps.approve.notes ?? '' }),
    },
  )
  .exit('unapproved', ctx => !ctx.steps.approve.approved)
  .step('send', sendReply, ctx => ({
    ticketId: ctx.unit.attributes.ticketId,
    reply: ctx.steps.approve.editedReply ?? ctx.steps.draft.reply,
  }), { afterCrash: 'park' })
  .exit('sent');

const handleEscalation = H.flow('handle-escalation')
  .input(escalation)
  .halt('handle', escalationHandled, {
    ask: ctx => `Ticket ${ctx.unit.attributes.ticketId} escalated (${ctx.unit.attributes.reason}): ${ctx.unit.attributes.subject}`,
  })
  .exit('handled', ctx => ctx.steps.handle.outcome === 'handled')
  .exit('dropped');

const helpdeskToken = H.env('ZENDESK_TOKEN');

const conversations = H.lane('conversations', Conversation)
  .supply(zendesk.webhook({ port: H.slot.port(2), path: '/helpdesk', secret: H.env('ZENDESK_WEBHOOK_SECRET') }), routeTicket)
  .supply(zendesk.poll({ subdomain: 'acme', token: helpdeskToken, everyMinutes: 10 }), routeTicket)
  .store(zendesk.store({ subdomain: 'acme', token: helpdeskToken }))
  .handler(reply, { exits: { sent: Sent, unapproved: Escalated } })
  .retry({ maxAttempts: 3, backoff: 'exponential', initialDelayMs: 30000, exhausted: Escalated })
  .ceiling({ maxUsd: 0.4, halt: costCeiling })
  .on(customerReplied, { update: (attrs, payload) => ({ ...attrs, message: payload.message }), enter: New })
  .on(customerClosed, { enter: ClosedByCustomer })
  .on(slaBreached, { update: attrs => ({ ...attrs, escalationReason: 'SLA breached' }), enter: Escalated });

const escalations = H.lane('escalations', Escalation)
  .handler(handleEscalation, { exits: { handled: EscalationHandled, dropped: EscalationDropped } })
  .retry({ maxAttempts: 1, exhausted: EscalationDropped });

const slaBreach = H.trigger('sla-breach-escalates')
  .on(H.when.timer(conversations, { in: New, at: unit => new Date(unit.attributes.slaDeadline) }))
  .signal(slaBreached, conversations, event => ({ key: event.unit.key, payload: {} }));

const openEscalation = H.trigger('escalated-conversation-opens-escalation')
  .on(H.when.transition(conversations, { to: Escalated }))
  .create(escalations, event => ({
    ticketId: event.unit.attributes.ticketId,
    subject: event.unit.attributes.subject,
    reason: event.unit.attributes.escalationReason ?? 'reply not approved or handling failed',
  }));

const tasteJournal = H.journal('support-taste', H.memory('taste', 'taste'))
  .store(jsonl.memoryStore({ path: '.harness/taste.jsonl' }))
  .recall({ by: 'specificity', limit: 10 })
  .readBy(drafter)
  .recordedBy(reviewer);

const experienceJournal = H.journal('support-experience', H.memory('experience', 'experience'))
  .store(jsonl.memoryStore({ path: '.harness/experience.jsonl' }))
  .recall({ by: 'specificity', limit: 10 })
  .readBy(drafter)
  .recordedBy(reviewer);

const reviewerTaste = H.trigger('reviewer-notes-become-taste')
  .on(H.when.decision(Conversation, approval))
  .record(tasteJournal, event =>
    event.resolvedBy === 'human' && event.decision.notes
      ? { text: event.decision.notes, status: 'candidate', when: { roles: [drafter] } }
      : undefined);

const scheduler = H.scheduler('support')
  .fixedDate(conversations, unit => new Date(unit.attributes.slaDeadline))
  .standard(escalations);

const supervisor = claudeCode.supervisor('reviewer', {
  port: H.slot.port(1),
  grants: [
    H.ops.workRead,
    H.ops.workUpdate,
    H.ops.resolve(approval, costCeiling, escalationHandled),
    H.ops.memoryWrite,
    H.ops.memoryCurate,
    H.ops.telemetryRead,
  ],
});

const harness = H.harness('support-triage')
  .ledger(sqlite.ledger({ path: '.harness/ledger.db' }))
  .lanes(conversations, escalations)
  .journals(tasteJournal, experienceJournal)
  .triggers(slaBreach, openEscalation, reviewerTaste)
  .metrics(approvals)
  .scheduler(scheduler)
  .clients(supervisor)
  .observers(markdown.board({ path: 'BOARD.md' }), markdown.telemetry({ path: 'TELEMETRY.md' }));

void harness.start();
=== END ===

=== FILE: scenarios/03-research-pipeline.ts ===
import { z } from 'zod';
import { H } from 'harness-dsl';
import { anthropic } from 'harness-dsl/anthropic';
import { sqlite } from 'harness-dsl/sqlite';
import { jsonl } from 'harness-dsl/jsonl';
import { pgvector } from 'harness-dsl/pgvector';
import { voyage } from 'harness-dsl/voyage';
import { local } from 'harness-dsl/local';
import { http } from 'harness-dsl/http';
import { markdown } from 'harness-dsl/markdown';

const topic = z.object({ title: z.string(), question: z.string(), recurring: z.boolean() });

const Open = H.state('Open', 'pending');
const Delivered = H.terminal('Delivered', 'success');
const Parked = H.terminal('Parked', 'neutral');
const Cancelled = H.terminal('Cancelled', 'neutral');
const Failed = H.terminal('Failed', 'failure');
const Topic = H.kind('Topic').attributes(topic).states(Open, Delivered, Parked, Cancelled, Failed).key(a => a.title);

const quota = sqlite.quota('research-quota', { path: '.harness/quota.db' });
const apiAccount = anthropic.account('research-api', { apiKey: H.env('ANTHROPIC_API_KEY'), quota });
const api = H.pool('research-api').accounts(apiAccount);
const haiku = anthropic.model('haiku', { id: 'claude-haiku-4-5' });
const opus = anthropic.model('opus', { id: 'claude-opus-4-5' });
const opusPrior = anthropic.model('opus-prior', { id: 'claude-opus-4-1' });

const searcher = H.role('searcher').intents('search', 'browse').instructions('Search for sources on the angle given and extract claims with their source URLs.');
const synthesizer = H.role('synthesizer').intents('read').instructions('Write a sourced report. Cite every claim. Say when sources are insufficient.');

const synthesizerModel = H.policy.model('synthesizer-model', [opus, opusPrior], ({ seat, metrics }) => {
  const window = { lastDays: 60 };
  const current = metrics.rate(citationPass, { seat, model: opus, window });
  const rival = metrics.rate(citationPass, { seat, model: opusPrior, window });
  if (current.samples < 20) return opus;
  if (rival.samples < 20) return opusPrior;
  return rival.rate > current.rate ? opusPrior : opus;
});

const searcherSeat = H.seat('searcher')
  .role(searcher)
  .model(haiku)
  .pool(api)
  .output(z.object({ findings: z.array(z.object({ claim: z.string(), source: z.string() })) }));

const synthesizerSeat = H.seat('synthesizer')
  .role(synthesizer)
  .model(synthesizerModel)
  .pool(api)
  .output(z.object({
    sufficientSources: z.boolean(),
    report: z.string(),
    citations: z.array(z.string()),
    keyFindings: z.array(z.string()),
  }));

const citationCheck = H.command('check-citations')
  .input(z.object({ citations: z.array(z.string()) }))
  .argv(i => ['./bin/check-citations', ...i.citations])
  .runner(local.runner('local'));

const research = H.flow('research')
  .input(topic)
  .job('search', searcherSeat, ctx => Array.from({ length: 20 }, (_, index) => ({
    task: `Search angle ${index + 1} of 20 for: ${ctx.unit.attributes.question}`,
  })))
  .step('synthesize', synthesizerSeat, ctx => ({
    task: `Write a sourced report answering: ${ctx.unit.attributes.question}\n\n${ctx.steps.search
      .map(result => result.findings.map(f => `- ${f.claim} (${f.source})`).join('\n'))
      .join('\n')}`,
  }))
  .exit('parked', ctx => !ctx.steps.synthesize.sufficientSources)
  .step('citations', citationCheck, ctx => ({ citations: ctx.steps.synthesize.citations }))
  .exit('delivered');

const topicCost = H.halt('topic-cost').decision(H.ceilingDecision);

const topics = H.lane('topics', Topic)
  .supply(H.operator)
  .store(sqlite.store({ path: '.harness/topics.db' }))
  .handler(research, { exits: { parked: Parked, delivered: Delivered } })
  .retry({ maxAttempts: 2, backoff: 'exponential', initialDelayMs: 300000, exhausted: Failed })
  .ceiling({ maxUsd: 3, halt: topicCost })
  .on(H.cancel, { enter: Cancelled });

const citationPass = H.metric('citation-check-pass', H.when.step(topics, 'citations')).samples(event => [
  { hit: event.ok, seat: synthesizerSeat, model: event.modelOf(synthesizerSeat) },
]);
const researchSpend = H.metric('research-spend', H.when.invocation({ lanes: [topics] })).amounts(event => [
  { amount: event.costUsd },
]);
const succeededAttemptCost = H.metric('succeeded-topic-attempt-cost', H.when.transition(topics, { to: [Delivered, Parked] }))
  .amounts(event => (event.attempt ? [{ amount: event.attempt.costUsd }] : []));

const findingsJournal = H.journal('prior-findings', H.memory('report-findings', 'experience'))
  .store(pgvector.memoryStore({
    url: H.env('PGVECTOR_URL'),
    table: 'report_findings',
    embedder: voyage.embedder('voyage', { id: 'voyage-3', apiKey: H.env('VOYAGE_API_KEY') }),
  }))
  .recall({ by: 'similarity', limit: 8 })
  .readBy(synthesizer);

const sourceJournal = H.journal('source-lessons', H.memory('source-experience', 'experience'))
  .store(jsonl.memoryStore({ path: '.harness/sources.jsonl' }))
  .recall({ by: 'specificity', limit: 10 })
  .readBy(searcher, synthesizer);

const recordFindings = H.trigger('report-findings-become-memory')
  .on(H.when.step(topics, 'synthesize', { if: event => event.ok }))
  .record(findingsJournal, event =>
    event.output
      ? {
          text: `When researching a topic like "${event.unit.attributes.title}", start from these findings, because an earlier report established them: ${event.output.keyFindings.join('; ')}`,
          when: { kinds: [Topic] },
        }
      : undefined);

const reopenRecurring = H.trigger('reopen-recurring-topics')
  .on(H.when.timer(topics, {
    in: [Delivered, Parked],
    at: unit => (unit.attributes.recurring ? H.nextTime('08:00', { on: 'mon', tz: 'UTC', after: unit.createdAt }) : undefined),
  }))
  .create(topics, event => event.unit.attributes);

const scheduler = H.scheduler('research')
  .standard(topics)
  .admit(topics, ({ metrics }) => {
    const spentToday = metrics.total(researchSpend, { window: { calendar: 'day', tz: 'UTC' } });
    const succeeded = metrics.total(succeededAttemptCost, { window: { lastDays: 30 } });
    const projected = succeeded.samples > 0 ? succeeded.total / succeeded.samples : 3;
    return spentToday.total + projected <= 40;
  });

const operatorApi = http.controlApi('operator', {
  port: H.slot.port(1),
  token: H.env('RESEARCH_CONTROL_TOKEN'),
  grants: [
    H.ops.workRead,
    H.ops.workCreate,
    H.ops.workCancel,
    H.ops.resolve(topicCost),
    H.ops.memoryRead,
    H.ops.memoryWrite,
    H.ops.telemetryRead,
  ],
});

const harness = H.harness('research-pipeline')
  .ledger(sqlite.ledger({ path: '.harness/ledger.db' }))
  .lanes(topics)
  .journals(findingsJournal, sourceJournal)
  .triggers(recordFindings, reopenRecurring)
  .metrics(citationPass, researchSpend, succeededAttemptCost)
  .scheduler(scheduler)
  .clients(operatorApi)
  .observers(markdown.board({ path: 'BOARD.md' }), markdown.telemetry({ path: 'TELEMETRY.md' }));

void harness.start();
=== END ===

